drm/omap: no manual update with no plane to show

When a client's framebuffer is removed while it is shown (a KMS client
exiting), a commit disables the primary plane, and a manually updated
display was still sent an update. With no overlay enabled DISPC sends
nothing, FRAMEDONE never came, and after 250 ms the RFBI driver gave up
and dropped the tearing effect trigger for good ("FRAMEDONE not received
for 250ms", "no tearing effect signal"); the next commit (the console's
restore) re-enabled the plane. Intermittent, depending on how the
removal and the restore interleave. The display keeps its last frame:
complete such an update at once without sending anything.

diff -ruN a/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/omap_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/omap_crtc.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/omap_crtc.c	2026-10-26 10:40:30.753299512 +0100
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/omap_crtc.c	2026-10-26 10:40:30.753299512 +0100
@@ -56,6 +56,8 @@
 	 */
 	struct drm_rect rect_next, rect;
 	bool partial_next, partial, cropped;
+	/* the commit left no plane to show: nothing to send */
+	bool blank;
 };
 
 /* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@ -440,6 +442,17 @@
 		return;
 
 	/*
+	 * With no plane enabled (a client's framebuffer removed while shown)
+	 * DISPC sends nothing and FRAMEDONE never comes: after 250 ms RFBI
+	 * gave up and dropped the tearing effect for good. The display keeps
+	 * the last frame; complete the update without sending one.
+	 */
+	if (omap_crtc->blank) {
+		omap_crtc_complete_update(&omap_crtc->base);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/*
 	 * No update, no FRAMEDONE: complete the flip here. Clearing pending
 	 * alone dropped the flip's event, and the commit waiting for it was
 	 * never done, so every later one got -EBUSY.
@@ -737,6 +750,7 @@
 		 * The output's size follows the rectangle the plane was cropped
 		 * to, or goes back to the whole frame
 		 */
+		omap_crtc->blank = !crtc->state->plane_mask;
 		omap_crtc->partial = omap_crtc->partial_next;
 		omap_crtc->rect = omap_crtc->rect_next;
 		omap_crtc->partial_next = false;
